# hub — real-world examples

hub wraps git with GitHub superpowers (`alias git=hub`). It is the
predecessor of the official `gh` CLI — see the `gh` sheet for the modern tool.

## As a contributor to open-source

```sh
# clone your own project
git clone dotfiles
# -> git clone git://github.com/YOUR_USER/dotfiles.git

# clone another project
git clone github/hub
# -> git clone git://github.com/github/hub.git

# see the current project's issues
git browse -- issues
# -> open https://github.com/github/hub/issues

# open another project's wiki
git browse mojombo/jekyll wiki
# -> open https://github.com/mojombo/jekyll/wiki
```

## Example workflow for contributing to a project

```sh
git clone github/hub
cd hub
git checkout -b feature        # create a topic branch
# ( make changes ... )
git commit -m "done with feature"
git fork                       # fork the repo on GitHub
# -> git remote add YOUR_USER git://github.com/YOUR_USER/hub.git
git push YOUR_USER feature     # push to your new remote
git pull-request               # open a PR (editor opens for the message)
```

## As an open-source maintainer

```sh
# fetch from multiple trusted forks, even if not yet added as remotes
git fetch mislav,cehoffman

# check out a pull request for review (creates a branch with its contents)
git checkout https://github.com/github/hub/pull/134

# apply all commits from a PR directly to the current branch
git am -3 https://github.com/github/hub/pull/134

# cherry-pick a GitHub commit URL
git cherry-pick https://github.com/xoebus/hub/commit/177eeb8

# `am` can beat cherry-pick — it doesn't create a remote
git am https://github.com/xoebus/hub/commit/177eeb8
```

## Compare views and new repos

```sh
# open the GitHub compare view between two releases
git compare v0.9..v1.0

# copy the compare URL for a topic branch to the clipboard
git compare -u feature | xclip -selection clipboard   # (pbcopy on macOS)

# create a GitHub repo for a new project
git init
git add . && git commit -m "It begins."
git create -d "My new thing"
git push origin master
```
